# 1. Project Overview

**Project Name:** SENTINEL (Scalable, Extensible, Network Traffic Intelligence Layer)

**One-Line Description:** A distributed API Gateway with pluggable rate limiting algorithms (Token Bucket, Sliding Window Log, Fixed Window Counter, Sliding Window Counter) implemented using Redis Lua scripts for atomic distributed counting, with per-tenant configuration, circuit breaking, JWT authentication, and real-time analytics.

**Author:** Rohit Kumar Jarariya [1]

**Why This Name:** A sentinel guards a gate — this project guards your APIs.

---

# 2. Problem Statement

In microservice architectures, every public-facing API needs protection from:

- **Abuse** — A single user sending 10,000 requests/second to overload the system
- **Cost Control** — Free-tier users consuming same resources as paid users
- **Fairness** — One heavy user starving others of resources
- **DDoS Mitigation** — Automated attacks overwhelming services

Current solutions like Spring Cloud Gateway's built-in rate limiter only support **one algorithm (Token Bucket)** and have **limited configurability**. SENTINEL solves this by offering **4 pluggable algorithms** with **per-tenant, per-endpoint configuration**, all running in a **distributed** setup using **Redis Lua scripts** for atomic operations.

